Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:01:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 405/407] SableOS: privacy summary step after Wi-Fi

Adds a Privacy step after Wi-Fi that states Sable's privacy defaults in
six short paragraphs: Sable apps send no analytics (LineageOS statistics
stay a separate choice on the LineageOS features step), accounts and
their data stay with their providers, Sable Hub reads notifications and
not accounts, any app can be blocked from the network, Android shows
notification content on the lock screen until the user hides it, and
restore uses Android's backup app.

Under the paragraphs it belongs to, each link opens the Settings screen
that controls it: Network access (org.sableos.settings.NETWORK_MANAGER),
lock screen notifications (Lock screen settings, else Notifications) and
Privacy. A link is shown only when its screen exists on the build
(SableLinks). The step changes no setting, Next is always enabled, and
Back/Esc return to Wi-Fi.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FqvfFQhAvko2gkqcxM25Aa
